div><p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/nyc/">New York</a> / Corrugated signs for planned short-term use</p><p class="eyebrow">VISION GRAPHICS · NEW YORK</p><h1>Corrugated signs for planned short-term use</h1><p class="lead">Corrugated plastic signs can be a practical format for temporary messages, events and property marketing when the application suits a lightweight panel. The important choices include how the sign will be supported, which sides need printing and how long it is expected to remain in place. Vision Graphics can help New York businesses and organizers plan the artwork around those conditions. Start with a concise message and an approved display location so production decisions follow the actual use rather than a standard-size assumption.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/nyc/contact/?product=Corrugated%20signs%20for%20planned%20short-term%20use">Discuss your project <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="#options">Explore options <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></div><figure class="project-image product-photo"><img src="/nyc/assets/mcs-new-service-custom-signs-960.webp" srcset="/nyc/assets/mcs-new-service-custom-signs-480.webp 480w, /nyc/assets/mcs-new-service-custom-signs-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 50vw" alt="Signage example related to Corrugated signs for planned short-term use" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Illustrative sign example · Michigan Custom Signs source</figcaption></figure></section><section class="wrap section article-layout"><article><section><h2>Keep the panel easy to understand</h2><p>Use a clear heading and only the information needed at the viewing distance. Small temporary signs can become crowded quickly, especially when several logos or disclaimers are included. Confirm the final wording and any required attribution before preparing the production layout.</p></section><section><h2>Match support to the setting</h2><p>Explain whether the panel will be mounted, placed in a holder or displayed on an approved ground support. Orientation and construction should be reviewed against the chosen method. Exposure and display life influence suitability; this format is not a substitute for a permanent structural sign.</p></section><section id="options"><p class="eyebrow">MATERIALS &amp; APPROACHES</p><h2>Find the right fit.</h2><div class="options-grid"><div><h3>Single-sided panels</h3><p>Focus the message toward one primary approach.</p></div><div><h3>Double-sided layouts</h3><p>Make a message visible from two directions where placement allows.</p></div><div><h3>Coordinated sign sets</h3><p>Keep event or property information consistent across several locations.</p></div><div><h3>Yard and ground-supported panels</h3><p>Plan a concise temporary message with a compatible support and an authorized location; ground placement is reviewed for the actual setting.</p></div></div></section><section><h2>Where it can work</h2><ul class="check-list"><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Temporary event directions</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Property marketing</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Approved campaign displays</li></ul></section><section class="faqs"><h2>A few useful answers.</h2><details><summary>Is corrugated signage intended to be permanent?<span>+</span></summary><p>It is commonly considered for temporary uses. The actual material and support should be selected for the planned conditions and duration.</p></details><details><summary>Can I print both sides?<span>+</span></summary><p>Two-sided layouts can be scoped. Confirm whether each side should match or serve a different direction of approach.</p></details></section></article><aside class="product-aside"><p class="eyebrow">LET’S START WITH THE DETAILS</p><h3>Have a space in mind?</h3><p>A photo, a few measurements and your project ZIP help us ask the right questions.</p><a href="/nyc/contact/?photo=1" class="btn dark"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-camera" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.997 4a2 2 0 0 1 1.76 1.05l.486.9A2 2 0 0 0 18.003 7H20a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V9a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h1.997a2 2 0 0 0 1.759-1.048l.489-.904A2 2 0 0 1 10.004 4z"></path><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3"></circle></svg> Send a project photo</a><hr><h3>Related possibilities</h3><a href="/nyc/political-signs/">Political signs<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="